General: Visibly distressed, lying supine, guarded movements. No gross neurological deficits.
Physical Exam: Significant paraspinal muscle spasm. Extreme reduction in lumbar flexion Schober test modified. Bilateral sacroiliac joint tenderness on palpation. Achilles tendon insertion tenderness bilaterally. Findings heavily favor early axial spondyloarthritis. Lower limb neurology intact; normal perianal sensation.
Environmental Observations: Slippery rugs in hallway noted; distance to bathroom poses an immediate fall risk.
